: "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 80 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Kathy Castor (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Florida's 14th District became genuinely competitive after redistricting, shifting from a safe Democratic seat to one with a slight Republican lean. Kathy Castor, a long-serving incumbent, faces former state Representative Mike Beltran, who has run a well-funded campaign and holds a slight cash-on-hand advantage. A July poll showed Castor ahead by eight points, but it is the only public survey and is now months old.\n\nExpert ratings split between toss-up and lean Democratic, with the overall consensus at lean Democratic, and Polymarket prices Castor's chances around 64 percent. The national political environment favors Democrats this cycle, and Washington is paying attention: the DCCC is running ads attacking Beltran's record in the legislature, and national Democrats are stumping in Florida's battleground seats. Castor's name recognition, fundraising, and the favorable environment give her the edge, but Beltran's resources keep the race within reach.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7914, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7727, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.766, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7799, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6958, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7726, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7812, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.75, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7285, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7934, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7587, "margin": 4.0}]}